8. Hybrid Feasible Domain

8.1 Corrected Active Authority

The minimum downward active force is

F_{\rm active,max}^-\ge \max_{(v,g)\in\mathcal D_{\rm design}}\bigl(F_{\rm PMEDS}(v,g)-mg\bigr).

Numerically, the required downward force at the extremes of the design domain is

F_{\rm active,max}^- \ge \max\{4.4,\,6.6,\,7.0\}\,\text{kN}\approx 7.0\,\text{kN}.

The earlier value of 4 kN is insufficient. The updated reference design uses F_{\rm active,max}^-=8 kN.

Sustained vs peak authority. The RMS force (limited by I^2R heating) is a separate constraint:

F_{\rm active,RMS}\le F_{\rm active,max}^{\rm RMS}\approx 0.7F_{\rm active,max}^-.

The peak force is required only during transients; the sustained force is required for steady-state cruise.

8.2 Hybrid Feasible Domain

\boxed{
\mathcal D_H=\left\{(v,g,\sigma):
\begin{aligned}
&g\in[g_{\min},g_{\max}],\\
&F_{\rm PMEDS}(v,g)+F_{\rm active,max}^+\ge mg\ \text{or}\ F_G\ge mg,\\
&P_D(v,g)\le P_{\max},\\
&\text{reachability constraint satisfied if}\ \sigma_{\rm cmd}\ \text{transitioning.}
\end{aligned}\right\}
}

8.3 Existence

Theorem 8.1. \mathcal D_H\neq\varnothing if and only if there exists g\in[g_{\min},g_{\max}] such that

F_\infty(g)+F_{\rm active,max}^+>mg

and

P_D^\infty(g)\le P_{\max}

and the reachability constraint admits a feasible trajectory.

Proof. The set \{g:F_\infty(g)+F_{\rm active,max}^+>mg\} is open because F_\infty is continuous and strictly decreasing. Intersecting with the closed power constraint and the reachability constraint gives a non-empty set if the inequalities are jointly satisfiable. ∎

8.4 Numerical Verification

At g=20 mm:

F_\infty(0.020)=8707\,\text{N},\qquad mg=4905\,\text{N},\qquad F_\infty/mg=1.775.

Downward authority required at v=8 m/s: F_{\rm PMEDS}(8,0.020)-mg\approx 8383-4905=3478 N. The reference 8 kN authority exceeds this, so \mathcal D_H\neq\varnothing.

At v=30 m/s, g=15 mm:

F_{\rm PMEDS}(30,0.015)\approx F_\infty(0.015)\approx 11920\,\text{N},

required downward force \approx 11920-4905=7015 N. The 8 kN authority covers this with margin.

