10.5 Final Statement

The tyre-free ground-level PMEDS architecture is a coherent physical concept whose control theory is now mathematically closed at the reduced-order level. The corrected stability analysis shows that active damping is not optional but structurally required, with a certified bound. The safety envelope is expressed in the correct barrier-function framework for each constraint, with the appropriate relative degree and nonsmoothness handling. Fault tolerance is formulated as discriminating-kernel inclusion under an augmented fault model with quantified fault timing. The remaining work is numerical construction of the hybrid feasible domain and the discriminating kernel, followed by experimental validation on a 100-metre demonstrator.

The architecture is now falsifiable. It survives the stability analysis of Chapter 3 only under the certified damping bound, survives the safety analysis of Chapter 6 only under the corrected relative degrees, and survives the fault-tolerance analysis of Chapter 7 only under the discriminating-kernel formulation. Any of these can be falsified by the numerical gates, and any falsification invalidates the corresponding claim.

