Appendix B: Averaging Error Bound

B.1 Instantaneous Force on the Array

The total instantaneous vertical force on the array is

F_y^{\rm tot}(t)=-k\phi_0\sum_{j=1}^{N}I_j(t)\cos\theta_j(t),\qquad \theta_j(t)=k(x_j-vt),

where x_j=jd_c. Each I_j=A\cos\theta_j+B\sin\theta_j, so

F_y^{\rm tot}(t)=-k\phi_0\sum_j\bigl(A\cos^2\theta_j+B\sin\theta_j\cos\theta_j\bigr).

Using \cos^2\theta=(1+\cos 2\theta)/2 and \sin\theta\cos\theta=\sin 2\theta/2:

F_y^{\rm tot}(t)=-\frac{k\phi_0 A}{2}N-\frac{k\phi_0}{2}\sum_j\bigl(A\cos 2\theta_j+B\sin 2\theta_j\bigr).

The first term is N\langle F_y\rangle. The oscillatory term is bounded by the modulus of the Dirichlet kernel.

B.2 Dirichlet Bound

Assume commensurate spacing kd_c=2\pi/m with m\in\mathbb N so that N=N_H m. Then \theta_j=2\pi j/m-\omega t and

\sum_{j=1}^{N}e^{2i\theta_j}=e^{-2i\omega t}\sum_{j=1}^{N_H m}e^{4\pi ij/m}.

The inner sum cycles every m indices with \sum_{j=1}^{m}e^{4\pi ij/m}=0 (since 4\pi/m is not a multiple of 2\pi for m>2). Therefore the sum telescopes and equals zero exactly. For m=1,2 or incommensurate spacing, the modulus is bounded by the Dirichlet kernel D_N(\cdot) uniformly in N, giving O(1).

Result. There exists a constant C depending only on geometry such that

\bigl|F_y^{\rm tot}(t)-N\langle F_y\rangle\bigr|\le C\,|k\phi_0|\sqrt{A^2+B^2}.

Dividing by N|\langle F_y\rangle|:

\boxed{\frac{\bigl|F_y^{\rm tot}-\overline{F_y^{\rm tot}}\bigr|}{|\overline{F_y^{\rm tot}}|}\le\frac{C}{N_H m}}.

For the reference parameters N_H=6, m=4, giving a relative error bound of C/24\approx 4\% for C\approx 1.

B.3 Gap Derivative Error

From F_M(v,g)=F_\infty(g)/(1+(v_t/v)^2) with F_\infty\propto e^{-2kg}:

\frac{\partial \ln F_M}{\partial g}=-2k\cdot\frac{1}{1+(v_t/v)^2}+2k\cdot\frac{(v_t/v)^2}{1+(v_t/v)^2}
=-2k\cdot\frac{1-(v_t/v)^2}{1+(v_t/v)^2}.

Wait — direct computation gives

\frac{\partial}{\partial g}\left[\frac{e^{-2kg}}{1+(v_t/v)^2}\right]=-\frac{2ke^{-2kg}}{1+(v_t/v)^2},

so

\frac{\partial \ln F_M}{\partial g}=-2k

exactly, without correction. The correction appears only in the instantaneous force (not the averaged one) when the array's field itself is modulated by the gap at the moment of induction. For the averaged force used in the control model:

\boxed{\frac{\partial \ln F_M}{\partial g}=-2k\ \text{exactly for the averaged force}}.

B.4 High-Speed Convergence Rate

F_M(v,g)-F_\infty(g)=-\frac{F_\infty(g)}{1+(v/v_t)^2}\cdot\frac{v_t^2}{v^2}=-\frac{F_\infty(g)(v_t/v)^2}{1+(v_t/v)^2},

so

\bigl|F_M-F_\infty\bigr|\le F_\infty(g)\Bigl(\frac{v_t}{v}\Bigr)^2.

B.5 Existence and Uniqueness of the Periodic Solution

The circuit ODE is linear with a T-periodic forcing. The homogeneous solution decays as e^{-(R/L)t}=e^{-t/\tau_e}. The periodic solution exists uniquely for every v>0 and every initial condition converges to it exponentially with rate 1/\tau_e.

