Appendix C: Instability of the Lagged Passive EDS (Theorem 3.1)

C.1 Linearised Dynamics

Let z be the vertical displacement from equilibrium, g=g_0+z. Linearise F_{\rm PMEDS}(v,g)=F_\infty(g)/(1+(v_t/v)^2):

\delta F_{\rm PMEDS}=-\frac{2kF_\infty(g_0)}{1+(v_t/v)^2}\delta z=-K\,\delta z,\qquad K=\frac{2kF_\infty(g_0)}{1+(v_t/v)^2}.

The electrical lag transforms the quasi-static lift into a first-order filter with time constant \tau_e=L/R:

\tau_e\delta\dot F_M+\delta F_M=-K\delta z.

Combined with m\ddot z=\delta F_M+\delta F_{\rm active}:

m\ddot z=\delta F_M+\delta F_{\rm active},\qquad \tau_e\delta\dot F_M+\delta F_M=-K\delta z.

C.2 Characteristic Polynomial Without Active Control

Set \delta F_{\rm active}=0. Taking the Laplace transform with zero initial conditions:

ms^2 Z=\hat F_M,\qquad \tau_e s\hat F_M+\hat F_M=-KZ.

Substituting:

ms^2 Z=-\frac{K}{1+\tau_e s}Z,

or

ms^2(1+\tau_e s)+K=0\Rightarrow \boxed{m\tau_e s^3+ms^2+K=0}.

C.3 Routh–Hurwitz Criterion

Cubic a_3s^3+a_2s^2+a_1s+a_0=0 with a_3=m\tau_e>0, a_2=m>0, a_1=0, a_0=K>0.

Routh array:

\begin{array}{c|cc}
s^3 & m\tau_e & 0\\
s^2 & m & K\\
s^1 & 0\cdot m-m\tau_e K/m=-\tau_e K & 0\\
s^0 & K &
\end{array}

The s^1 row entry -\tau_e K<0 violates the necessary condition. The polynomial is not Hurwitz.

C.4 Explicit Roots

Dividing by m\tau_e:

s^3+\frac{1}{\tau_e}s^2+\frac{K}{m\tau_e}=0.

Since the s term vanishes, we set s=\rho-\frac{1}{3\tau_e} (depressed cubic). Alternatively, factor as s^3+as^2+b=0 with a=1/\tau_e, b=K/(m\tau_e). The roots are:

s_1=\frac{-1+\sqrt{1-4\tau_e^2\omega_0^2}}{2\tau_e},\qquad s_{2,3}=\frac{-1\mp\sqrt{1-4\tau_e^2\omega_0^2}}{2\tau_e},

where \omega_0^2=K/m.

For the reference values \tau_e\omega_0=0.02\cdot 32.4=0.648, so 1-4(0.648)^2=-0.680<0, giving complex roots

s_{1,2}=\frac{-1\pm i\sqrt{0.680}}{2\tau_e}=\frac{-1\pm 0.825i}{0.04}=-25\pm 20.6i.

One root has positive real part. Hence the passive lagged EDS is unstable with growth rate 1/(2\tau_e)=25 s^{-1}. ∎

