Appendix D: Minimal Damping Bound (Theorem 3.3)

D.1 Closed-Loop Characteristic Polynomial

With PD active control U=-k_pz-k_d\dot z and actuator lag \tau_F:

m\ddot z=\delta F_M+\frac{1}{\tau_F s+1}U,\qquad \tau_e s\hat F_M+\hat F_M=-KZ.

Taking the Laplace transform and substituting:

ms^2 Z=-\frac{K}{1+\tau_e s}Z-\frac{k_p+k_ds}{1+\tau_F s}Z.

Multiplying through by (1+\tau_e s)(1+\tau_F s):

ms^2(1+\tau_e s)(1+\tau_F s)+K(1+\tau_F s)+(k_p+k_ds)(1+\tau_e s)=0.

Expanding:

m\tau_e\tau_F s^4+m(\tau_e+\tau_F)s^3+(m+k_d\tau_e)s^2+(K\tau_F+k_d+k_p\tau_e)s+(K+k_p)=0.

Define

a_4=m\tau_e\tau_F,\quad a_3=m(\tau_e+\tau_F),\quad a_2=m+k_d\tau_e,\quad a_1=K\tau_F+k_d+k_p\tau_e,\quad a_0=K+k_p.

D.2 Routh–Hurwitz Conditions

Routh array for a quartic:

\begin{array}{c|cc}
s^4 & a_4 & a_2 & a_0\\
s^3 & a_3 & a_1 & 0\\
s^2 & b_1 & b_2 & 0\\
s^1 & c_1 & 0 & 0\\
s^0 & a_0 & &
\end{array}

with

b_1=\frac{a_3a_2-a_4a_1}{a_3},\qquad b_2=\frac{a_3a_0}{a_3}=a_0,\qquad c_1=\frac{b_1a_1-a_3a_0}{b_1}.

Necessary and sufficient conditions: all a_i>0, b_1>0, c_1>0.

D.3 Sufficient Condition for k_d

For simplicity take k_p=0. Then:

b_1=\frac{m(\tau_e+\tau_F)(m+k_d\tau_e)-m\tau_e\tau_F(K\tau_F+k_d)}{m(\tau_e+\tau_F)}
=\frac{(m+k_d\tau_e)(\tau_e+\tau_F)-\tau_e\tau_F(K\tau_F+k_d)}{\tau_e+\tau_F}.

For small k_d: b_1\to (m(\tau_e+\tau_F)-\tau_e\tau_FK\tau_F)/(\tau_e+\tau_F), which can be negative if K\tau_e\tau_F^2 is large. For our parameters K\tau_e\tau_F^2=0.263 and m(\tau_e+\tau_F)=12.5, so b_1>0 automatically. Hence the binding condition is c_1>0.

Substituting a_i:

c_1=a_1-\frac{a_3a_0}{b_1}=\frac{(K\tau_F+k_d)b_1-m(\tau_e+\tau_F)K}{b_1}.

Numerator:

N_c=(K\tau_F+k_d)b_1-m(\tau_e+\tau_F)K.

Using the explicit form of b_1:

N_c=\frac{(K\tau_F+k_d)[(m+k_d\tau_e)(\tau_e+\tau_F)-\tau_e\tau_F(K\tau_F+k_d)]}{\tau_e+\tau_F}-m(\tau_e+\tau_F)K.

Multiplying by (\tau_e+\tau_F):

N_c(\tau_e+\tau_F)=(K\tau_F+k_d)(m+k_d\tau_e)(\tau_e+\tau_F)-(K\tau_F+k_d)\tau_e\tau_F(K\tau_F+k_d)-m(\tau_e+\tau_F)^2K.

For the reference values, we solve N_c=0 numerically. Expanding in powers of k_d, the leading quadratic term is

(k_d)(k_d\tau_e)(\tau_e+\tau_F)-k_d^2\tau_e\tau_F=k_d^2\tau_e[(\tau_e+\tau_F)-\tau_F]=k_d^2\tau_e^2>0.

The linear coefficient is K\tau_F\tau_e(\tau_e+\tau_F)-K\tau_e\tau_F^2=\tau_e\tau_F(\tau_e+\tau_F-\tau_F)K=K\tau_e^2\tau_F.

The constant term is (K\tau_F)m(\tau_e+\tau_F)-K\tau_F\tau_e\tau_FK\tau_F-m(\tau_e+\tau_F)^2K, which is negative for our parameters. Solving k_d^2\tau_e^2+K\tau_e^2\tau_F k_d-(\text{const})=0:

k_d^{\min}=\frac{-K\tau_e^2\tau_F+\sqrt{K^2\tau_e^4\tau_F^2+4\tau_e^2\cdot\text{const}}}{2\tau_e^2}.

Numerically: K\tau_e^2\tau_F=526000\cdot 4\times 10^{-4}\cdot 5\times 10^{-3}=1.05, \text{const}\approx m(\tau_e+\tau_F)^2K-mK\tau_F(\tau_e+\tau_F)+K^2\tau_e\tau_F^3\approx 500\cdot 6.25\times 10^{-4}\cdot 526000-500\cdot 526000\cdot 5\times 10^{-3}\cdot 0.025+526000^2\cdot 0.02\cdot 1.25\times 10^{-7}. Evaluating: 164375-32875+692\approx 132192.

Then 4\tau_e^2\text{const}=4\times 4\times 10^{-4}\times 132192=211.5, so \sqrt{1.1+211.5}=14.6. Thus

k_d^{\min}=\frac{-1.05+14.6}{8\times 10^{-4}}\approx 1.69\times 10^4\ \text{N·s/m}.

Simplified conservative bound. Since K\tau_e\tau_F\ll m, the dominant terms give

\boxed{k_d^{\min}\approx 2\sqrt{mK}\cdot\frac{\tau_e+\tau_F}{2\sqrt{\tau_e\tau_F}}=\sqrt{mK}\cdot\frac{\tau_e+\tau_F}{\sqrt{\tau_e\tau_F}}}.

Numerically \sqrt{500\cdot 526000}\cdot 0.025/\sqrt{10^{-4}}=16220\cdot 2.5=40550. The conservative bound overestimates; the sharper value is k_d^{\min}\approx 1.7\times 10^4 N·s/m. ∎

D.4 Closed-Loop Bandwidth

The dominant pole of the closed loop is bounded by the sum of the two lags:

\omega_{\rm cl}\le\frac{1}{\tau_e+\tau_F}=40\ \text{rad/s}.

The ECBF design bandwidth \omega_n must satisfy \omega_n\le\omega_{\rm cl}/2\approx 20 rad/s for robust phase margin.

